t mirror symmetric, up-down mirror symmetric, or 180-degree-rotation-only symmetric.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/3.py:200:    - Detect every grey room, locate its unique doorway gap, and classify the symmetry of the interior floor-pattern mask inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/3.py:441:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/3/3.py:184:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/3/3.py:424:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/3.py:117:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/3.py:316:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/6.py:89:                \"grey\": int(dominant),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/6.py:197:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/6.py:203:    - Near the left edge there is a vertical grey ruler whose single-pixel colored tick marks interrupt the grey line at different heights.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/6.py:230:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/2.py:129:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/2.py:348:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:139:        assert np.array_equal(bottom_mask, np.flipud(top_mask)), \"vertical pair must be horizontal mirrors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:152:        assert np.array_equal(right_mask, np.fliplr(left_mask)), \"horizontal pair must be vertical mirrors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:163:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:164:    \"\"\"Pair same-colored fragments and slide each mirrored pair together until they form one symmetric figure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:167:    - The background is azure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:169:    - The two fragments of a color are mirror images of each other across a horizontal or vertical axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:178:    - Color identifies the pairing, while shared row-band or column-band alignment reveals the mirror axis and therefore the direction in which the two asymmetric pieces must close toward the middle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:281:    mirrored = np.flipud(mask) if axis == \"vertical\" else np.fliplr(mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:283:        first_mask, second_mask = mask, mirrored\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:285:        first_mask, second_mask = mirrored, mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:371:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/9/2.py:383:    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid mirrored-fragment puzzle\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:53:def _grey_color(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> int:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:61:def _parse_legend(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, grey: int) -> tuple[dict[tuple[int, int], int], np.ndarray]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:63:    color_mask = (grid != bg) & (grid != grey)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:96:    grey: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:111:        assert int(grid[cr, cc]) == grey, \"marker paths must enter grey channels before any junction\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:128:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:130:    Slide colored dead-end markers along grey channels until they reach their first junction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:139:    - Treat grey cells together with the non-legend marker pixels as the channel network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:140:    - For each marker, follow its unique branch through grey cells until the first grey cell whose network degree is at least three.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:141:    - Recolor every traversed grey channel cell with the marker's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:142:    - If exactly one marker reaches a junction, recolor that junction with the marker color; if exactly two markers reach it, use the legend's color-mixing lookup; untouched junctions stay grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:149:    grey = _grey_color(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:151:    mix_map, legend_mask = _parse_legend(g, bg, grey)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:152:    marker_mask = (g != bg) & (g != grey) & (~legend_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:153:    network_mask = (g == grey) | marker_mask\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:161:        trail, junction = _trace_marker(start, g, grey, network_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:174:            out[r, c] = grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/2.py:368:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/4.py:103:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/4.py:111:    - In each label row, green marks mean \"left neighbor exists\", \"upper neighbor exists\", and \"right neighbor exists\"; grey marks absent directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/4.py:321:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:71:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:76:    - The background is black. A single full-width grey row splits the grid into an upper code panel and a lower strip of four canvases.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:77:    - The upper panel has odd height and contains one odd-sized square code window whose center cell is grey; four non-grey colors occupy quarter-turn-related pixel sets around that center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:78:    - The lower panel has the same height as the code window side length and consists of four equal square canvases separated by grey columns; each canvas is otherwise black except for a one-pixel color marker at its top-left corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:83:    - Output only the lower strip: keep the grey separator columns, clear the marker pixels, place the selected color pattern centered in each canvas, and paint the grey center cell of every canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:103:    assert center_positions.shape[0] == 1, \"expected one grey rotation center in the upper panel\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/11/4.py:237:def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/5.py:237:def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/12/5.py:239:    Move each scattered monochrome block into the bottom container whose grey icon shows the same shape family